/-!
# The twisted relation sheaf of generating sections of an invertible sheaf

Let `L` be an invertible sheaf of modules on a ringed space whose stalks are local rings, and let
`s : I → Γ(X, L)` be global sections generating `L`. They induce `π : O_X^{⊕I} ⟶ L`, whose kernel
`F` is the sheaf of relations among the `s i`. This file proves Tag 0B3B: `F ⊗ L` is generated by
global sections, namely by the Koszul sections `e_i ⊗ s_j − e_j ⊗ s_i`.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.tmulSection`: the global section `m ⊗ n` of `F ⊗ G` determined by global
  sections of the two factors.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.koszulSection`: the Koszul global section `e_i ⊗ s_j − e_j ⊗ s_i` of
  `O_X^{⊕I} ⊗ L`.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.koszulKernelSection`: the same section read in the kernel of `π ⊗ 1_L`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.kernelTensorGeneratingSections`: **Tag 0B3B** — generating global
  sections of `F ⊗ L`.

## Implementation notes

The statement is for a ringed space all of whose structure-sheaf stalks are local rings, that is
for a locally ringed space, which is the generality Stacks itself records for this lemma; a scheme
is such a space. The index type of the generating family is arbitrary, since the relation argument
never uses finiteness.

The proof runs through the kernel of `π ⊗ 1_L` rather than through `F ⊗ L` directly. Tensoring
with an invertible sheaf is an equivalence of categories, hence preserves kernels, so the two
agree; `CategoryTheory.Limits.PreservesKernel.iso` is that comparison and
`SheafOfModules.GeneratingSections.equivOfIso` transports the conclusion back. The gain is that
the Koszul sections are visibly global sections of `O_X^{⊕I} ⊗ L`, whereas no expression for them
as a global section of `F ⊗ L` is available before the comparison is made.

That the Koszul sections are killed by `π ⊗ 1_L` is the statement that `s_i ⊗ s_j = s_j ⊗ s_i` in
`L ⊗ L`. This is checked on stalks, where `L` is free of rank one by the converse half of Tag
0B8M, and the tensor square of a rank-one module is symmetric by
`Stacks.SelfBraidingInvertible.tmul_comm_of_rankOne`.

Heartbeats are counted cumulatively over a declaration, so a budget overrun is relieved by
splitting the declaration, not by cheapening any one step inside it. The two stalk-level
computations here are split accordingly: `ker_stalkMapL_tensorSheafMap_id`, `stalkMapL_pi_basis`
and `span_range_symm` carry the parts of `span_koszul_germ_eq_ker_stalkMapL` that do not mention
the Koszul family, and `stalkMapL_grpGerm` and `tensorStalkIso_germ_koszulSection` the two halves
of `stalkMapL_kernel_ι_germ_koszulKernelSection`. The first three are stated at a variable sheaf,
a variable basis and a variable linear equivalence, which is what keeps the long sheaf
expressions out of them.

The ring index of every sheaf of modules fed to `Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor` is
written out: `SheafOfModules.free (R := structureSheafRing X)`, and
`SheafOfModules.unit (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf ⟨X.presheaf, X.IsSheaf⟩)`. Left to
the elaborator, the same free sheaf comes out at `structureSheafRing X` under `tensorStalkIso`
and at `Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf ⟨X.presheaf, X.IsSheaf⟩` under `sheafTensor`;
the two are definitionally equal but not syntactically so, which both hides the module
instance on a tensor stalk from instance search and stops the rewrites of one statement from
matching the other. The unit sheaf is written at the tensor's own ring index because that is
what `SheafOfModules.unitHomEquiv` produces there.

`Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf` is a plain `def`, so a term applying `sheafTensor` to
a sheaf of modules indexed by `structureSheafRing X` is not type-correct at `implicit`
transparency — the transparency at which `rw`'s `kabstract` checks the goal. The six proofs
that rewrote through such a term are therefore `Eq.trans` chains of `congrArg`s, which are
checked by unification at `default` transparency instead: the two halves of
`ker_stalkMapL_tensorSheafMap_id`, the end of `span_koszul_germ_eq_ker_stalkMapL`,
`app_tensorSheafMap_koszulSection`, the last step of
`sectionsMap_kernel_ι_koszulKernelSection`, `stalkMapL_kernel_ι_germ_koszulKernelSection`, and
the `hmap` step of `kernelTensorGeneratingSections`. The last two also stay inside the
cumulative heartbeat budget only in that form. Where the stalk of a tensor object needs its
module structure, `Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorStalkRingedSpace.stalkModule` is named at that
object, as `tensorStalkIso` does in its own statement; no instance is declared here.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B3B](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B3B)
-/
@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits TensorProduct
open Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorStalkRingedSpace

universe u

/-! ### Basis transport along a ring isomorphism -/

namespace Module.Basis

variable {R S M ι : Type*} [Ring R] [Ring S] [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M] [Module S M]

/-- A basis of `M` over `S` is a basis of `M` over `R`, when the ring isomorphism `e : S ≃+* R`
identifies the two scalar actions. -/
noncomputable def ofRingEquiv (e : S ≃+* R) (he : ∀ (s : S) (m : M), e s • m = s • m)
    (b : Module.Basis ι S M) : Module.Basis ι R M :=
  Module.Basis.ofRepr
    (AddEquiv.toLinearEquiv
      (b.repr.toAddEquiv.trans (Finsupp.mapRange.addEquiv e.toAddEquiv)) (fun r m => by
        have hr : r • m = e.symm r • m := by
          rw [← he (e.symm r) m, RingEquiv.apply_symm_apply]
        refine Finsupp.ext fun i => ?_
        rw [hr]
        change e (b.repr (e.symm r • m) i) = r * e (b.repr m i)
        rw [map_smul, Finsupp.smul_apply, smul_eq_mul, map_mul, RingEquiv.apply_symm_apply]))

/-- `Module.Basis.ofRingEquiv` has the same members as the basis it transports. -/
@[simp] theorem ofRingEquiv_apply (e : S ≃+* R) (he : ∀ (s : S) (m : M), e s • m = s • m)
    (b : Module.Basis ι S M) (i : ι) : Module.Basis.ofRingEquiv e he b i = b i := by
  classical
  have h1 : (Module.Basis.ofRingEquiv e he b).repr (b i) = Finsupp.single i (1 : R) := by
    refine Finsupp.ext fun j => ?_
    show e (b.repr (b i) j) = (Finsupp.single i (1 : R)) j
    rw [b.repr_self, Finsupp.single_apply, Finsupp.single_apply]
    by_cases hij : i = j
    · simp [hij]
    · simp [hij]
  exact (Module.Basis.ofRingEquiv e he b).repr.injective
    (((Module.Basis.ofRingEquiv e he b).repr_self i).trans h1.symm)

end Module.Basis

namespace Stacks.SheafOfModules

variable (X : AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSpace.{u, u})

section TensorSections

variable (F G : SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheafRing X))

/-! ### Global sections of a tensor product -/

/-- `toTensorSheafSection` is additive, so it commutes with differences. -/
theorem toTensorSheafSection_sub (U : (TopologicalSpace.Opens X.carrier)ᵒᵖ)
    (t t' : TensorProduct (X.presheaf.obj U) (F.val.obj U) (G.val.obj U)) :
    toTensorSheafSection X F G U (t - t')
      = toTensorSheafSection X F G U t - toTensorSheafSection X F G U t' :=
  map_sub ((sheafifyUnit X ((PresheafOfModules.tensorObj (O := (X).presheaf) (F.val) (G.val)))).app
      U).hom t t'

/-- Restricting a section of `F ⊗ G` that comes from the presheaf tensor product is the image of
the restriction: the sheafification unit `toTensorSheafSection` is natural. -/
theorem map_toTensorSheafSection {U V : (TopologicalSpace.Opens X.carrier)ᵒᵖ} (f : U ⟶ V)
    (t : TensorProduct (X.presheaf.obj U) (F.val.obj U) (G.val.obj U)) :
    (((((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u, u, u, u, u}
        (⟨X.presheaf, X.IsSheaf⟩ : Sheaf (JX X) CommRingCat.{u})).obj (F)).obj (G))).val.map f).hom
        (toTensorSheafSection X F G U t)
      = toTensorSheafSection X F G V ((((PresheafOfModules.tensorObj (O := (X).presheaf) (F.val)
          (G.val))).map f).hom t) :=
  congrArg (fun q => q.hom t) ((sheafifyUnit X ((PresheafOfModules.tensorObj (O := (X).presheaf)
      (F.val) (G.val)))).naturality f).symm

/-- The global section `m ⊗ n` of `F ⊗ G` determined by global sections `m` of `F` and `n` of
`G`: over an open `U` it is the image of `m|_U ⊗ n|_U` under the canonical map
`F(U) ⊗_{O_X(U)} G(U) → (F ⊗ G)(U)`. -/
noncomputable def tmulSection (m : F.sections) (n : G.sections) :
    ((((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u, u, u, u, u}
        (⟨X.presheaf, X.IsSheaf⟩ : Sheaf (JX X) CommRingCat.{u})).obj (F)).obj (G))).sections :=
  PresheafOfModules.sectionsMk
    (fun U => toTensorSheafSection X F G U (m.eval U ⊗ₜ[X.presheaf.obj U] n.eval U))
    (by
      intro U V f
      have h := map_toTensorSheafSection X F G f (m.eval U ⊗ₜ[X.presheaf.obj U] n.eval U)
      have hm := PresheafOfModules.sections_property m f
      have hn := PresheafOfModules.sections_property n f
      change ((F.val).restrictₛₗ (f)) (m.eval U) = _ at hm
      change ((G.val).restrictₛₗ (f)) (n.eval U) = _ at hn
      change (((((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u, u, u, u, u}
          (⟨X.presheaf, X.IsSheaf⟩ : Sheaf (JX X) CommRingCat.{u})).obj (F)).obj (G))).val.map
          f).hom
          (toTensorSheafSection X F G U (m.eval U ⊗ₜ[X.presheaf.obj U] n.eval U))
        = toTensorSheafSection X F G V
          (((F.val).restrictₛₗ (f)) (m.eval U) ⊗ₜ[X.presheaf.obj V] ((G.val).restrictₛₗ (f))
              (n.eval U)) at h
      rw [hm, hn] at h
      exact h)

/-- Over an open `U`, the section `m ⊗ n` is the image of `m|_U ⊗ n|_U` in `(F ⊗ G)(U)`. -/
@[simp]
theorem tmulSection_eval (m : F.sections) (n : G.sections)
    (U : (TopologicalSpace.Opens X.carrier)ᵒᵖ) :
    (tmulSection X F G m n).eval U
      = toTensorSheafSection X F G U (m.eval U ⊗ₜ[X.presheaf.obj U] n.eval U) :=
  rfl
end TensorSections

variable (L : SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheafRing X))

/-! ### Germs of the generating sections -/

/-- The germ at `x` of the `i`-th tautological global section of the free sheaf of modules on
`I`. These germs are a basis of the stalk (`Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_basis_freeGerm`). -/
noncomputable abbrev freeGerm (I : Type u) (x : X.carrier) (i : I) :
    grpStalk X (_root_.SheafOfModules.free (R := structureSheafRing X) I).val x :=
  grpGerm X (_root_.SheafOfModules.free (R := structureSheafRing X) I).val x ⊤ (by simp)
    ((_root_.SheafOfModules.freeSection i).eval (Opposite.op ⊤))

/-- The germ at `x` of the `i`-th member of a family `g` of generating global sections of `L`. -/
noncomputable abbrev sGerm (g : L.GeneratingSections) (x : X.carrier) (i : g.I) :
    grpStalk X L.val x :=
  grpGerm X L.val x ⊤ (by simp) ((g.s i).eval (Opposite.op ⊤))

/-- **The germs of a generating family span the stalk.** This is
`AlgebraicGeometry.generates_iff_stalkwise_generates` read over the `CommRingCat`-valued stalk
ring `ringStalk`, which the identification of the stalk of a tensor product is stated over. -/
theorem span_sGerm_eq_top (g : L.GeneratingSections) (x : X.carrier) :
    Submodule.span (ringStalk X x) (Set.range (sGerm X L g x)) = ⊤ := by
  have hRaw : Submodule.span
      (R := (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (X := X.carrier) (structureSheafRing X).obj x : RingCat))
      (Set.range (sGerm X L g x)) = ⊤ := by
    have h := (AlgebraicGeometry.generates_iff_stalkwise_generates
      (O_X := structureSheafRing X) (F := L) g.s).mp g.epi x
    simp only [TopCat.Presheaf.Γgerm] at h
    exact h
  exact span_eq_top_of_ringEquiv _ _ (SemilinearStalk.commStalkRingEquiv X.presheaf x)
    (fun r m => commStalk_smul_eq X L.val x r m) _ hRaw

/-- **The germs of the tautological sections of a free sheaf of modules are a basis of its
stalk**, over the `CommRingCat`-valued stalk ring `ringStalk`. This is
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_stalkBasis_germ_freeSection` transported along
`SemilinearStalk.commStalkRingEquiv`. -/
theorem exists_basis_freeGerm (I : Type u) (x : X.carrier) :
    ∃ b : Module.Basis I (ringStalk X x)
        (grpStalk X (_root_.SheafOfModules.free (R := structureSheafRing X) I).val x),
      ∀ i, b i = freeGerm X I x i := by
  obtain ⟨b₀, hb⟩ := exists_stalkBasis_germ_freeSection (O := structureSheafRing X) I x
  refine ⟨Module.Basis.ofRingEquiv (SemilinearStalk.commStalkRingEquiv X.presheaf x)
    (fun r m => commStalk_smul_eq X
      (_root_.SheafOfModules.free (R := structureSheafRing X) I).val x r m)
    (b₀ : Module.Basis I
      (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (X := X.carrier) (structureSheafRing X).obj x : RingCat)
      (grpStalk X (_root_.SheafOfModules.free (R := structureSheafRing X) I).val x)),
    fun i => ?_⟩
  exact (Module.Basis.ofRingEquiv_apply _ _ _ i).trans (hb i)

/-- **Germ-naturality of the canonical linear stalk map.** The stalk of `φ` carries the germ of
a section to the germ of its image.

Stated at variable presheaves of modules: the equality holds by definition, but the two spellings
of the stalk functor's action on germs are identified only at `default` transparency, and that
reduction is taken here once, at variables, rather than at each of the long sheaf expressions the
lemma is used with. See the module docstring. -/
private theorem stalkMapL_grpGerm (M N : PresheafOfModules.{u} (O X)) (φ : M ⟶ N)
    (x : X.carrier) (U : TopologicalSpace.Opens X.carrier) (hx : x ∈ U)
    (m : M.obj (Opposite.op U)) :
    stalkMapL X M N φ x (grpGerm X M x U hx m)
      = grpGerm X N x U hx ((φ.app (Opposite.op U)).hom m) :=
  TopCat.Presheaf.stalkFunctor_map_germ_apply' U x hx
    ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf (O X)).map φ) m

/-- A morphism of sheaves of modules maps the evaluation of a global section at `U` to the
evaluation of the image section, whenever the image section is known. -/
private theorem app_eval_of_sectionsMap_eq {M N : SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheafRing X)}
    (f : M ⟶ N) {s : M.sections} {t : N.sections} (h : _root_.SheafOfModules.sectionsMap f s = t)
    (U : (TopologicalSpace.Opens X.carrier)ᵒᵖ) : (f.val.app U).hom (s.eval U) = t.eval U :=
  congrArg (fun t : N.sections => t.eval U) h

/-- The stalk of `g.π` carries the germ of the `i`-th tautological section of the free sheaf to
the germ of the `i`-th generating section. -/
theorem stalkMapL_pi_freeGerm (g : L.GeneratingSections) (x : X.carrier) (i : g.I) :
    stalkMapL X (_root_.SheafOfModules.free (R := structureSheafRing X) g.I).val L.val g.π.val x
        (freeGerm X g.I x i)
      = sGerm X L g x i :=
  (stalkMapL_grpGerm X _ _ g.π.val x ⊤ (by simp) _).trans
    (congrArg (grpGerm X L.val x ⊤ (by simp))
      (app_eval_of_sectionsMap_eq X g.π
        (_root_.SheafOfModules.sectionsMap_freeHomEquiv_symm_freeSection (M := L) (f := g.s)
          (i := i)) _))

/-- The stalk of the identity morphism is the identity. -/
theorem stalkMapL_id (x : X.carrier) :
    stalkMapL X L.val L.val (𝟙 L : L ⟶ L).val x = LinearMap.id := by
  ext m
  show stalkMap X L.val L.val (𝟙 L.val) x m = m
  unfold stalkMap
  rw [CategoryTheory.Functor.map_id, CategoryTheory.Functor.map_id]
  rfl

/-- `Stacks.SheafOfModules.commStalk_smul_eq` read through the inverse isomorphism: the
`CommRingCat`-valued scalar action on a stalk agrees with the `RingCat`-valued one. Stating it
for an arbitrary presheaf of modules keeps the module instance opaque, which matters at the call
site, where the stalk is that of a kernel. -/
theorem commStalk_symm_smul_eq (M : PresheafOfModules.{u} (O X)) (x : X.carrier)
    (r : ringStalk X x) (m : grpStalk X M x) :
    (SemilinearStalk.commStalkRingEquiv X.presheaf x).symm r • m = r • m := by
  have h := commStalk_smul_eq X M x ((SemilinearStalk.commStalkRingEquiv X.presheaf x).symm r) m
  rw [RingEquiv.apply_symm_apply] at h
  exact h.symm

/-- **The kernel of the stalk of `π ⊗ 1_L`, read through `tensorStalkIso`.** The stalk of a
tensor product is the tensor product of the stalks, and under that identification the stalk of
`π ⊗ 1_L` is `π_x ⊗ id`; so the kernel of the former is the preimage of the kernel of the
latter.

Stated at a variable sheaf of modules `F` rather than at the free sheaf `O_X^{⊕I}`, and split off
from `Stacks.SheafOfModules.span_koszul_germ_eq_ker_stalkMapL`: this reduction and the span
computation that consumes it are each well inside the heartbeat budget and only their total is
not. See the module docstring. -/
private theorem ker_stalkMapL_tensorSheafMap_id
    (F : SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheafRing X)) (π : F ⟶ L) (x : X.carrier) :
    letI := stalkModule X (((((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u, u, u, u, u}
        (⟨X.presheaf, X.IsSheaf⟩ : Sheaf (JX X) CommRingCat.{u}))).obj (F)).obj (L))).val x
    letI := stalkModule X (((((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u, u, u, u, u}
        (⟨X.presheaf, X.IsSheaf⟩ : Sheaf (JX X) CommRingCat.{u}))).obj (L)).obj (L))).val x
    LinearMap.ker (stalkMapL X ((((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u, u, u, u, u}
        (⟨X.presheaf, X.IsSheaf⟩ : Sheaf (JX X) CommRingCat.{u})).obj (F)).obj (L))).val
        ((((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u, u, u, u, u}
        (⟨X.presheaf, X.IsSheaf⟩ : Sheaf (JX X) CommRingCat.{u})).obj (L)).obj (L))).val
        (((Functor.uncurry.obj (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u, u, u, u, u}
            (⟨X.presheaf, X.IsSheaf⟩ : Sheaf (JX X) CommRingCat.{u}))).map
            ((π, (𝟙 L)) : (F, L) ⟶ (L, L)))).val x)
      = Submodule.comap ((tensorStalkIso X x F L).toLinearMap)
          (LinearMap.ker (TensorProduct.map (stalkMapL X F.val L.val π.val x)
            (LinearMap.id : grpStalk X L.val x →ₗ[ringStalk X x] grpStalk X L.val x))) := by
  let := stalkModule X (((((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u, u, u, u, u}
      (⟨X.presheaf, X.IsSheaf⟩ : Sheaf (JX X) CommRingCat.{u}))).obj (F)).obj (L))).val x
  let := stalkModule X (((((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u, u, u, u, u}
      (⟨X.presheaf, X.IsSheaf⟩ : Sheaf (JX X) CommRingCat.{u}))).obj (L)).obj (L))).val x
  have hnat := tensorStalkIso_natural X x F L L L π (𝟙 L)
  rw [stalkMapL_id X L x] at hnat
  ext z
  have hz := LinearMap.congr_fun hnat z
  simp only [LinearMap.comp_apply, LinearEquiv.coe_coe] at hz
  simp only [LinearMap.mem_ker, Submodule.mem_comap, LinearEquiv.coe_coe]
  rw [hz]
  exact (tensorStalkIso X x L L).map_eq_zero_iff.symm

/-- The stalk of `g.π` carries a basis member of the free sheaf's stalk to the germ of the
corresponding generating section, for any basis whose members are the germs of the tautological
sections. -/
private theorem stalkMapL_pi_basis (g : L.GeneratingSections) (x : X.carrier)
    (b : Module.Basis g.I (ringStalk X x)
      (grpStalk X (_root_.SheafOfModules.free (R := structureSheafRing X) g.I).val x))
    (hb : ∀ i, b i = freeGerm X g.I x i) (i : g.I) :
    stalkMapL X (_root_.SheafOfModules.free (R := structureSheafRing X) g.I).val L.val
        g.π.val x (b i)
      = sGerm X L g x i := by
  rw [hb i]
  exact stalkMapL_pi_freeGerm X L g x i

/-- **A span of pulled-back vectors is the pull-back of the span.** For a linear equivalence `e`
and a family `f` in its codomain, the span of `e.symm ∘ f` is the image under `e.symm` of the
span of `f`. -/
private theorem span_range_symm {R M N ι : Type*} [CommRing R] [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M]
    [AddCommGroup N] [Module R N] (e : M ≃ₗ[R] N) (f : ι → N) :
    Submodule.span R (Set.range fun i ↦ e.symm (f i))
      = Submodule.map (e.symm : N →ₗ[R] M) (Submodule.span R (Set.range f)) := by
  rw [Submodule.map_span, ← Set.range_comp]
  rfl

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0B3B (stalk-level heart).** At a point of a ringed space with local
stalks, the germs of the Koszul relations `e_i ⊗ s_j - e_j ⊗ s_i` span the kernel of the stalk
of `π ⊗ 1_L`, where `π = g.π` is the epimorphism from the free sheaf determined by a family `g`
of global sections generating the invertible sheaf `L`. -/
theorem span_koszul_germ_eq_ker_stalkMapL
    [∀ x : X.carrier, IsLocalRing (ringStalk X x)]
    [Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.presheaf (structureSheafRing X).property L]
    (g : L.GeneratingSections) (x : X.carrier) :
    letI := stalkModule X (((((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u, u, u, u, u}
        (⟨X.presheaf, X.IsSheaf⟩ : Sheaf (JX X) CommRingCat.{u}))).obj
        ((_root_.SheafOfModules.free (R := structureSheafRing X) g.I))).obj (L))).val x
